/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# The fresh-build-and-recopy step AGENTS.md's own loop calls for leaves a binary here; it
# is a build artifact of that workflow, never a source the workflow reads.
/nomos.exe

# Scratch build roots for generated projections. A projection is a rebuild artifact and
# most of them stay one: nothing here is a canonical source, and a registration may only
# name a record under docs/records, so a generated file cannot become one by accident.
#
# The exception is deliberate and narrow. A projection this repository *promises to ship*
# is committed together with its .nomos-projection.json stamp, and the gate re-derives it
# and fails if the pair has drifted -- `nomos spec freshness --require <profile>`. Which
# outputs those are is repository publication policy, named at the gate step rather than
# here, because a profile describes how a projection is built and not whether anybody
# ships it.
/build/
/release-artifacts/
.nomos/

# Local coordination state. Claims, leases and heartbeats are ephemeral and must not
# become high-frequency git changes; `work/ledger.json` itself IS committed, because
# its readability under `git diff` is load-bearing for the multi-agent workflow.
/work/*.lock
/work/*.tmp

# Local Cargo configuration, including the opt-in sibling-development override
# `.cargo/xvpe-local.toml` that redirects the pinned XVPE crossing to a local checkout.
# `OD-PLATFORM-004` records its status: the pinned git dependency in each manifest is the
# only governing form, and nothing here carries any authority. Excluded mechanically rather
# than by care, because this working tree is shared with live sessions and an untracked
# file in it is one scoped `git add` away from being published as though it were the
# decided form.
#
# The whole directory, not one filename. `config.toml` is the name Cargo discovers on its
# own, so a file left there substitutes the sibling checkout into every command any session
# in this tree runs. Ignoring only the override's own name would leave that name free to be
# recreated, which is the shape this refinement exists to remove. A build resolved through
# any of it is development-resolved rather than reproducible.
/.cargo/
.claude/settings.local.json
